# SEO, metadata and public pages

Search engines and link previews read these pages before any user does. Every rule here has a matching file in `src/app/` that already exists. Edit it, don't recreate it.

## 1. Title and description on every page

Must:
- Export `metadata` or `generateMetadata` from every `page.tsx`, including admin, auth and error pages.
- Give each page a unique `title` and a `description` of 120 to 160 characters that says what the page offers.
- Keep the root layout's `title.template` (`%s | <site name>`) from `site.config.ts`, so pages set only their own part.
- Take the site name, URL, tagline and contact details from `siteConfig`. Never repeat them as literals.
- Set `alternates.canonical` on public pages.
- Set `robots: { index: false, follow: false }` on admin, account, auth and thank-you pages.

```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: PRIVACY_COPY.META_TITLE,
  description: PRIVACY_COPY.META_DESCRIPTION,
  alternates: { canonical: ROUTES.PRIVACY },
};
```

## 2. Site files

| File | Purpose | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `app/robots.ts` | robots.txt | Disallows `/admin`, `/account` and the auth routes. Points to the sitemap. |
| `app/sitemap.ts` | sitemap.xml | Lists every public route with `lastModified`. Add a route here in the same change that creates the page. |
| `app/manifest.ts` | Web app manifest | Name, colors and icons from `siteConfig`. |
| `app/icon.png`, `app/apple-icon.png` | Favicon and Apple touch icon | Replace the image files when rebranding. Don't add `<link>` tags by hand. |
| `app/opengraph-image.tsx` | Default Open Graph image, 1200 by 630 | Renders the site name and tagline from `siteConfig`. Pages with their own share image add an `opengraph-image.tsx` in their folder. |
| `app/not-found.tsx` | Custom 404 | Has a heading, a short explanation and links home and to login. Server pages call `notFound()` to reach it. |

Must:
- Set `metadataBase` in the root layout from `siteConfig.url`, so Open Graph URLs resolve.
- Set `openGraph` and `twitter` (`summary_large_image`) defaults in the root layout.

## 3. Landing page

Must:
- Put the headline, one supporting sentence and the primary CTA in the hero. The CTA must be visible without scrolling at 375 by 667 and at 1280 by 800.
- Point the primary CTA at one action, which is register by default, using `ROUTES`.
- Keep the section order: hero, features, how it works, FAQ, footer.
- Show `StickyMobileCta` below the `md` breakpoint once the hero scrolls out of view. Add bottom padding to the page so the bar never covers the footer links.
- Add FAQ structured data (`FAQPage` JSON-LD) built from the same copy constant that renders the FAQ.
- Render marketing sections as server components. The sticky CTA and the mobile menu are the only client components.

Never:
- Put a carousel or autoplay video in the hero.
- Add a second competing primary CTA above the fold.

## 4. Images

Must:
- Use `next/image` for every image.
- Write `alt` text that describes what the image shows or does. Use `alt=""` only for decorative images.
- Set `sizes` on responsive images, so the browser downloads the right width.
- Add `priority` only to the largest image above the fold.
- Compress static images before committing them. Use WebP or AVIF for photos, SVG for logos and icons, and keep photos under about 200 KB.
- Give images explicit `width` and `height`, or `fill` inside a sized container, so the layout doesn't shift while they load.

Never:
- Use a plain `<img>` tag.
- Commit uncompressed PNG or JPEG photos.
- Write alt text such as "image" or "photo", or repeat the file name.

## 5. Public pages

| Route | Content |
|---|---|
| `/privacy` | Privacy policy using `siteConfig` for the company name and contact email. Marked as a template the project must replace. |
| `/terms` | Terms and conditions, same pattern as privacy. |
| `/thank-you` | Shown after registration. Tells the user to check their inbox for the verification email, offers a resend button (a `LoadingButton` with cooldown) and links to login. Not indexed. |

Must:
- Link Privacy and Terms from the footer and from the register form.
- Show a "last updated" date on legal pages.

## 6. Performance

Must:
- Load fonts with `next/font` in the root layout.
- Keep public pages static. Avoid `cookies()`, `headers()` and `no-store` fetches in marketing routes.
- Avoid client-side JavaScript on public pages beyond the sticky CTA, the mobile menu and the theme toggle.

Never:
- Load third-party scripts without `next/script` and a `strategy`.

## Review checklist

- [ ] Every new page exports `metadata` or `generateMetadata` with a unique title and a 120 to 160 character description.
- [ ] Private pages set `robots: { index: false }`. Public pages set a canonical URL.
- [ ] New public routes are in `sitemap.ts`. Private routes are disallowed in `robots.ts`.
- [ ] Site name, URL and contact details come from `siteConfig`.
- [ ] The hero CTA is visible without scrolling at 375 and 1280 px, and the sticky mobile CTA works.
- [ ] Every image uses `next/image` with meaningful `alt`, `sizes` and dimensions. Static images are compressed.
- [ ] Privacy and Terms are linked from the footer and the register form.
- [ ] Marketing pages stay static and server-rendered.
